# =============================================================================
# Long Island Spine and Orthopedics — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. In production set these in Vercel under
# Settings -> Environment Variables (Production AND Preview).
#
# `.env.local` and `.env` are both gitignored. If a real secret is ever
# committed, rotating it is the only fix — the git history keeps the old value
# forever.
#
# Every variable is listed. Anything marked REQUIRED must be set before the
# corresponding feature works; the app degrades loudly rather than silently
# when one is missing. docs/BACKEND.md explains what each subsystem does when
# its variables are absent.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site identity
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Deployment mode: "portfolio" (default) or "production".
#
# DEFAULTS TO PORTFOLIO WHEN UNSET, MISSPELLED OR EMPTY. That is deliberate —
# see the note in lib/siteMode.ts. Portfolio mode adds `noindex, nofollow` at
# three layers (meta tag, X-Robots-Tag header, robots.txt disallow) and does
# nothing else: same design, same copy, same forms, same backend.
#
# This is the control that matters. An unindexed site is not reachable by a
# patient searching for an orthopedic surgeon, so the only visitors are people
# who were handed the URL.
#
# Do not set this to "production" until the launch blockers in docs/BACKEND.md
# have real answers — the office email address, the legal review, and the HIPAA
# determination. Note also that Vercel's Hobby plan is restricted to personal,
# non-commercial use; a live practice site needs a paid plan.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_MODE="portfolio"

# Set to exactly "1" to render the visible "portfolio demonstration" band in
# the site chrome. OFF by default, and deliberately independent of the mode
# above so a cosmetic choice cannot disable the noindex.
#
# Worth turning on for exactly one combination: an INDEXED deployment carrying
# this practice's real telephone number whose appointment form does not yet
# reach someone who reads it. With noindex on, it reaches nobody who needs it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PORTFOLIO_NOTICE=""

# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. The public origin, no trailing slash.
#
# Feeds the canonical tags, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, the JSON-LD graph and the
# admin deep links inside office emails — see lib/siteUrl.ts. Unset, everything
# falls back to http://localhost:3000, which makes share previews fail visibly
# in development instead of silently pointing production somewhere wrong.
#
# [PLACEHOLDER: production domain] — BUILD-BRIEF.md Part 6, Step 1.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://example.com"


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — Neon Postgres
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Pooled connection string from the Neon dashboard.
#
# Use the POOLED host (it contains `-pooler`). The unpooled one exhausts
# connections quickly under serverless, where every invocation is a new client.
# Keep `?sslmode=require`.
#
# Also read by `npm run db:migrate`. Point it at a branch, not production, when
# trying a migration out.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx-pooler.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Encryption
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. 32 bytes, base64. Generate with:
#
#     openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Encrypts the patient's free-text notes and the staff internal notes
# (lib/crypto/field.ts, AES-256-GCM).
#
# LOSING THIS MAKES EVERY STORED NOTE PERMANENTLY UNREADABLE. There is no
# recovery path and no escrow; the rest of each row still decodes, and the
# notes render as unavailable. Keep a copy somewhere that is not this
# repository and not the same password manager entry as DATABASE_URL.
#
# Changing it has the same effect on rows already written. The ciphertext
# carries a `v1.` prefix so a future rotation can decrypt old rows with the old
# key while writing new ones with the new — that migration does not exist yet.
FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# RECOMMENDED. Any long random string; `openssl rand -base64 32` is fine.
#
# Salts the HMAC that turns a submitter's IP into a fingerprint for rate
# limiting and abuse review (lib/security/hash.ts). The raw address is never
# stored. Unset, a well-known development salt is used, which makes the hashes
# reversible by anyone who reads this repository.
IP_HASH_SALT=""


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email — Resend
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED for any mail to be sent. https://resend.com -> API Keys.
# Unset, both notification emails and the admin magic link are skipped with a
# warning in the logs. Submissions are still saved.
RESEND_API_KEY=""

# REQUIRED alongside the API key. The From address, on a domain verified in
# Resend. Verify the domain and add its DKIM/SPF/DMARC records first, or the
# mail lands in spam (BUILD-BRIEF.md Part 6, Step 5).
MAIL_FROM="Long Island Spine and Orthopedics <no-reply@example.com>"

# REQUIRED for the office to be notified. Where appointment requests and
# enquiries are delivered, and the Reply-To on the patient's confirmation.
#
# [PLACEHOLDER: office email address] — BUILD-BRIEF.md Part 0 lists this as a
# launch blocker. Unset, the office notification is skipped and logged; the
# submission is still saved and still appears in /admin.
OFFICE_EMAIL="appointments@example.com"


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin access — Auth.js
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Signs the session cookie. Generate with:
#
#     npx auth secret
#
# Changing it signs every member of staff out.
AUTH_SECRET=""

# REQUIRED. Comma-separated addresses allowed to sign in to /admin.
#
# THIS IS THE ENTIRE ACCESS CONTROL LIST for the patient inbox. Empty or unset
# authorises NOBODY — it fails closed on purpose. Read on every request, so
# removing an address takes effect on that person's next click rather than when
# their session happens to expire.
ADMIN_EMAILS="frontdesk@example.com,manager@example.com"


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bot protection — Cloudflare Turnstile
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OPTIONAL but strongly recommended in production. https://dash.cloudflare.com
# -> Turnstile. Free.
#
# Both must be set for the check to run. With neither, the widget is not
# rendered and the server reports `skipped`, which is the local-development
# behaviour. With only the site key, the widget renders and the server ignores
# it — do not ship that.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=""
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=""


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limiting — Upstash Redis
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OPTIONAL but strongly recommended in production. https://upstash.com -> Redis
# -> REST API. Free tier is ample at this volume.
#
# Unset, the forms fall back to an in-process limiter that is per-instance and
# therefore close to useless on serverless — it exists so `npm run dev` works
# with an empty .env, and it warns on first use.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduled jobs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED for the 90-day retention purge. `openssl rand -base64 32`.
#
# Vercel Cron sends it as `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET`. Unset, the
# purge route refuses to run (HTTP 500) rather than deleting patient data with
# no authentication — but closed submissions then accumulate indefinitely,
# which is a retention-policy failure, so set it.
CRON_SECRET=""


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OPTIONAL. Set to exactly `vercel` to enable Vercel Analytics (cookieless).
# Anything else, including unset, loads no analytics at all.
#
# Do not substitute Google Analytics. See the note in components/site/Analytics.tsx
# — it changes what the privacy notice has to say on a medical site.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS=""


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test harness — never set this in production
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Set to `1` ONLY by playwright.config.ts. Swaps the database and the mailer
# for in-process test doubles so the end-to-end suite can drive a real
# submission with no Postgres and no Resend.
#
# It is ignored whenever NODE_ENV is `production`, which `next build` sets — so
# a production bundle cannot honour it however it is configured. That is why
# Playwright runs against `next dev`.
# E2E_TEST_MODE="1"
